---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Cinematic Celebration';
const description =
  'How Cinematic Celebration collects, uses, and protects your information when you use our website.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="bg-festive-animated -mx-4 rounded-3xl px-6 py-10 text-center text-white shadow-lg">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold drop-shadow sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
  </section>

  <article class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-4 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 text-gray-700 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <p>
      At Cinematic Celebration, we prioritize the privacy of our visitors. This
      Privacy Policy outlines the types of information we collect and how we use
      it. If you have any questions or need further information, please feel free
      to reach out to us.
    </p>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy applies exclusively to our online activities and
        pertains to information shared and collected on the Cinematic Celebration
        website. It does not extend to information collected offline or through
        channels other than our website.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Consent</h2>
      <p>
        By using our website, you consent to and agree with our Privacy Policy and
        its terms.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We collect personal information as needed, and the reasons will be stated
        at the time of collection. When you contact us directly, we may collect
        additional information including your name, email address, phone number,
        the contents of your messages, attachments, and any other information you
        choose to provide. When you register for an account, we may ask for
        contact information such as name, address, email address, and telephone
        number.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">How we use your information</h2>
      <ul class="ml-5 list-disc space-y-1">
        <li>Provide, operate, and maintain our website</li>
        <li>Enhance and customize your website experience</li>
        <li>Analyze and understand how you use our website</li>
        <li>Develop new products, services, features, and functionality</li>
        <li>Communicate with you for customer service, updates, and marketing</li>
        <li>Send you emails</li>
        <li>Identify and prevent fraud</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Log files</h2>
      <p>
        Cinematic Celebration follows industry-standard practices using log files.
        These record visitor data such as IP addresses, browser types, Internet
        Service Providers, date and time stamps, and referring/exit pages. This is
        used for trend analysis and site administration and is not linked to
        personally identifiable information.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Cookies and web beacons</h2>
      <p>
        Like other websites, we use cookies to store visitor preferences and track
        pages visited, to enhance the user experience by customizing content.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Third-party privacy policies</h2>
      <p>
        Our Privacy Policy does not apply to other advertisers or websites. We
        recommend consulting the respective privacy policies of any third-party ad
        servers for comprehensive information, including instructions for opting
        out of certain options.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Your privacy rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under applicable privacy laws, including the CCPA and GDPR, you have rights
        regarding your personal data:
      </p>
      <ul class="ml-5 mt-2 list-disc space-y-1">
        <li>Right to access — request copies of your personal data.</li>
        <li>Right to rectification — request corrections to your data.</li>
        <li>Right to erasure — request deletion of your data under certain conditions.</li>
        <li>Right to restrict processing under certain conditions.</li>
        <li>Right to object to processing under certain conditions.</li>
        <li>Right to data portability under certain conditions.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-2">
        If you wish to exercise these rights, please contact us. We will respond
        within one month. We value your privacy and are committed to protecting
        your data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
